 ;; ── the defect ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :defect-found-in-the-loop-itself
 {:symptom "h5-engine-pin -- a hypothesis kept deliberately as a MEASURED ZERO,
            landed 2026-08-17 and confirmed to change no served number -- was
            ranked LAST at -$6.78 per million. A control that reads as a loss."
  :cause
  "`workerd-scale` is 2397/1976: the measured level of 2026-08-18 morning over
   the harness level that produced it. The outer-string change then moved the
   measured level to 2058 without anyone re-running the harness. Every
   hypothesis carrying a stale `:after-harness {:cpu-ms 1976}` -- i.e. every
   hypothesis that claims NOT to move CPU -- was therefore scaled to 2397 and
   priced as a +339 ms regression it does not cause."
  :who-it-hit ["h3-engine-materialisation" "h4-carv2-pack" "h5-engine-pin"]
  :fix "`:after-harness {:cpu-ms :unchanged}` resolves to the LIVE baseline with
        no proxy in the path at all. A hypothesis that does not claim to move
        CPU is priced at the CPU that was actually measured."
  :evidence-the-fix-is-right
  {:before {:h5 -6.78 :h3 -6.64 :h4 0.42}
   :after  {:h5 0.0   :h3 0.0   :h4 7.2}
   :note "h5 is the control and it now reads exactly zero. h4's real saving --
          the 84->64 class-B reduction it always claimed -- was being cancelled
          by a CPU regression it never had, which is why iteration-02 read it as
          worth $0.42 and dismissed it."}
  :lesson "A calibration constant computed from two measurements decays when
           either one moves. The loop had a control in it precisely so this
           would be visible, and the control had been reporting the defect for a
           full iteration before anyone read it as one."}

 ;; ── generate: one new hypothesis ────────────────────────────────────────────
 :new-hypothesis
 {:id "h8-l2-cache-api"
  :found-by "reading the sibling Worker's block cache while answering an
             unrelated question about the storage layout"
  :the-asymmetry
  "kotobase-graph-database (datoms.kotobase.net) has had TWO cache tiers since
   its block cache landed -- L1 isolate memory and L2 the Cloudflare Cache API,
   which is per-colo and outlives the isolate. kotobase-protocols-worker had L1
   alone."
  :why-that-matters-here
  "Measured 2026-08-18: twelve consecutive reads of /_diag/hydrate reported
   `sampled: false` twelve times -- twelve isolates, none of which had ever
   hydrated. L1 is cold on every request anyone can measure. The 84 class-B
   gets and 11.46 MB in the baseline ARE that coldness, and they are $30.24 of
   the $71.70 unit cost -- 42%, in the term the roadmap had not been ranking."
  :basis :predicted
  :what-is-measured "the mechanism (L1 cannot help; the tier is absent here)"
  :what-is-not "the hit RATE. 75% is an assumption. 50% saves $15.12, 90% saves
                $27.36, and a measured zero is a possible outcome."
  :cpu :unchanged
  :cpu-note "A cache hit removes a ROUND TRIP, and cpuTime does not include I/O
             wait. Anyone expecting this to move the CPU term has mistaken which
             resource it buys."}

